Q can a instance variable or constructors in java interface?



Every field declared directly inside an interface is implicitly public static final.

public - The field is accessible from outside the interface.

static - The field belongs to the interface/class level, not to individual implementing objects.

final - The field cannot be reassigned after initialization. 


An interface cannot have a constructor because a constructor is used to initialize an object when it is created, while an interface cannot be instantiated directly. 
An interface only defines a contract that implementing classes must follow.
Therefore, object creation and initialization are handled by the constructor of the implementing class, not the interface.

